            {
                "entry_id": "455ab3b3-4cb6-3e34-a48e-5172cc5020ad",
                "word": "darse",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "7e5bea95-e2e8-4b47-aa4e-58790d360e4b",
                        "entry_id": "455ab3b3-4cb6-3e34-a48e-5172cc5020ad",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "darses"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "487a3291-b714-40ca-99e8-0633679dd530",
                        "entry_id": "455ab3b3-4cb6-3e34-a48e-5172cc5020ad",
                        "tags": [],
                        "form": "darce"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "35a25f9e-2f99-3e4d-9194-4aae95d0be8f",
                        "entry_id": "455ab3b3-4cb6-3e34-a48e-5172cc5020ad",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Partie intérieure des ports de la Méditerranée, où il n’y a pas de marée."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "cb14f0de-9397-45d0-be99-380f7bc9b48e",
                                "sense_id": "35a25f9e-2f99-3e4d-9194-4aae95d0be8f",
                                "text": "Ou, peut-être, n’était-il pas trop mécontent de pouvoir aller vivre à Toulon, traîner sur la darse, acagnarder sa passion de vieillard dans un coin de décor maritime, auprès de la « poule » dont parlait Victor ?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5d7bd126-1f2e-42a6-9a45-b9553fdbd44a",
                                "sense_id": "35a25f9e-2f99-3e4d-9194-4aae95d0be8f",
                                "text": "On voit encore une darse à moitié comblée qui pourrait bien avoir été l’Aphrodise."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c90b1dad-b17f-445e-b438-8e99c31a50b1",
                                "sense_id": "35a25f9e-2f99-3e4d-9194-4aae95d0be8f",
                                "text": "Deux balcons donnaient sur un petit port de pêche, la darse A du chenal sud, qui offrait quelque ressemblance avec Saint-Tropez, et sur une lagune aux odeurs fétides."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0d0da766-6a5c-381a-aa3e-6ae6fefeedf5",
                        "entry_id": "455ab3b3-4cb6-3e34-a48e-5172cc5020ad",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Bassin rectangulaire destiné principalement à l’accostage des cargos."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7547f5a3-f972-48c4-977f-a3cc9a1529e2",
                                "sense_id": "0d0da766-6a5c-381a-aa3e-6ae6fefeedf5",
                                "text": "Peu avant trois heures de l'après-midi, sur le Paseo de Colón, je montai dans l'autobus qui devait me mener à Montjuïc. Derrière la vitre se dressait la forêt de mâts et de pavillons qui flottaient dans la darse du port."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "efe7f533-11e7-387e-a6c1-aa89612e6a41",
                        "entry_id": "455ab3b3-4cb6-3e34-a48e-5172cc5020ad",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Structure de quai permettant à un élévateur à bateaux de se placer au-dessus d’une embarcation pour la sortir de l’eau."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b1a10e49-ed8c-4e38-bcec-fc070ef59077",
                        "source_entry_id": "455ab3b3-4cb6-3e34-a48e-5172cc5020ad",
                        "target_lang_word": "Dock",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Dock",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "04f1f9bd-f666-3251-af9b-f050d066bc28",
                                        "entry_id": "92d479a9-779c-342a-8381-340df5002ec8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Becken oder schwimmender Hohlkörper aus Stahl zur Trockenlegung von Schiffen, an denen Außenarbeiten erforderlich sind"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Schiffbau"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ac86f208-201a-460e-b1b0-5d917e88efec",
                                                "sense_id": "04f1f9bd-f666-3251-af9b-f050d066bc28",
                                                "text": "Auch im Dock ist schließlich höchste Präzision gefragt: Zwischen Bugwulst und Dockkopf dürfen nur zwei Meter Platz bleiben, damit am Heck der \"Queen\" genügend Raum zum Arbeiten an den Antrieben bleibt."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4b2771be-50d2-4c54-8065-485425db1364",
                                                "sense_id": "04f1f9bd-f666-3251-af9b-f050d066bc28",
                                                "text": "Die Londoner Docks wurden ursprünglich nur für Eisenbahnanschluß gebaut und haben bis heute keine ausreichenden Einrichtungen für den Lkw-Verkehr […]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ff705f8c-2b72-4836-987f-b07ce0e8d29e",
                                                "sense_id": "04f1f9bd-f666-3251-af9b-f050d066bc28",
                                                "text": "„Am südlichen Ende von Limehouse, in den Docks von Deptford, säumten Becken für Marine- und Handelsschiffe beide Ufer in östlicher Richtung.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b3019b14-9cfc-47f8-86a8-a49b55fc68f8",
                                                "sense_id": "04f1f9bd-f666-3251-af9b-f050d066bc28",
                                                "text": "„Die Docks würden bald ihre alte Bedeutung verlieren, weil sich Englands Handelswege mit der Welt jetzt schon völlig änderten.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "95c38bee-739b-40d4-a40f-3763e8bc750c",
                                                "sense_id": "04f1f9bd-f666-3251-af9b-f050d066bc28",
                                                "text": "„Die Gegend der Docks ist reizvoll, und viele Gebäude aus dem 17. und 18. Jahrhundert sind erhalten.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fef05e74-a5d6-48df-b4ef-85ee6e31359a",
                        "source_entry_id": "455ab3b3-4cb6-3e34-a48e-5172cc5020ad",
                        "target_lang_word": "wet dock",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "wet dock",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "96045a5f-46c4-3eb3-a7ed-ab9597753321",
                                        "entry_id": "ae60d381-5410-37e8-9a69-1f0a11343e29",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A dock that has a constant level of water in which a vessel floats despite the tide; usually achieved by separating the dock from the sea by a lock."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5bd67942-0ca3-4161-824e-b55f3f30e65b",
                                                "sense_id": "96045a5f-46c4-3eb3-a7ed-ab9597753321",
                                                "text": "1957, J. D. Salinger, \"Zooey\", in, 1961, Franny and Zooey, 1991 LB Books edition, page 90,\nIt was rather as though, after being in makeshift wet dock for days, the Queen Mary had just sailed out of, say, Walden Pond, as suddenly and perversely as she had sailed in."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "76b3c110-dd7d-4e6b-871e-0821374b3eed",
                        "source_entry_id": "455ab3b3-4cb6-3e34-a48e-5172cc5020ad",
                        "target_lang_word": "harbour",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "harbour",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "36e0b0db-74fb-37e6-abd1-f26e3f74ac00",
                                        "entry_id": "525efd52-3b49-3d43-be86-17bd433c1b52",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Standard spelling of harbor."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dd24f788-611a-4c38-9033-e822437bba7f",
                                                "sense_id": "36e0b0db-74fb-37e6-abd1-f26e3f74ac00",
                                                "text": "In West Wales it has never been possible until recently to exploit the magnificent natural harbour of Milford Haven, for there was no industrial hinterland."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "harbour",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "28cee849-a16b-379b-a0f1-4127d57d5000",
                                        "entry_id": "77778396-c6e2-38ef-8d0b-46038b0af79a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Standard spelling of harbor."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4a8d37ab-d56d-469e-9b01-577dec48dc59",
                                                "sense_id": "28cee849-a16b-379b-a0f1-4127d57d5000",
                                                "text": "The docks, which once harboured tall ships, now harbour only petty thieves."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b6fb7283-24fc-4f5b-b92d-46960c2d8d09",
                                                "sense_id": "28cee849-a16b-379b-a0f1-4127d57d5000",
                                                "text": "The bare suspicion made it treason to harbour the person suspected."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4bebf777-47ae-493f-b345-b115d86e5855",
                                                "sense_id": "28cee849-a16b-379b-a0f1-4127d57d5000",
                                                "text": "Nor let your gentle Breast harbor one Thought Of Outrage from the Kin."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "45293254-675d-43b7-84ec-13a8f426ccc2",
                                                "sense_id": "28cee849-a16b-379b-a0f1-4127d57d5000",
                                                "text": "Its streets fan out towards the clifftops, and its sheltered North Landing harbours open-decked fishing boats, called 'cobles'."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e5c2fc23-baba-4b73-bda4-ae1590387c83",
                                                "sense_id": "28cee849-a16b-379b-a0f1-4127d57d5000",
                                                "text": "If Moldova harboured even the slightest hopes of pulling off a comeback that would have bordered on miraculous given their lack of quality, they were snuffed out 13 minutes before the break"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
